{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121871","id":4154501179,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc73oKg7","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121871","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121871.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121871.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121871","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121871/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121871/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121871/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e42d3336db0a4ad26ed2f5dc6c96b314afb91a3a","number":121871,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add experimental .NET Web export support using static LibGodot","user":{"login":"wpbiggs","id":9951968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTE5Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9951968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs","html_url":"https://github.com/wpbiggs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\r\nBased on and preserving authorship from #118976 by @NoctemCat. This rebases the static LibGodot approach onto current `master` and refines the Web export integration.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- Adds experimental .NET Web export support using the standard .NET browser-wasm runtime and a statically linked LibGodot.\r\n- Supports threaded and non-threaded Web templates, C# ↔ JavaScript interop, AOT, cryptography, and `HttpClient`.\r\n- Packages the static engine, Emscripten configuration, JavaScript libraries, and pre/post-JS hooks in the Web template.\r\n- Adds the corresponding Godot .NET SDK browser props/targets and managed/native bridge.\r\n- Preserves the normal Web export lifecycle by extracting only the internal `libgodot` payload before export plugins run, then extracting regular HTML/JS template files in their established phase.\r\n- Fixes the Web/macOS build-output embedding condition after rebasing.\r\n- Updates the implementation for current `master`, including the current export notification API and Python 3.9 compatibility.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\nGodot 4 currently rejects C# Web exports. The .NET browser-wasm toolchain needs to own the final Emscripten link, while Godot normally produces a complete WebAssembly executable itself. Building Godot as a static library lets the .NET SDK link the managed application, .NET runtime, and engine into one WebAssembly module.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- Built a macOS .NET editor and generated/packaged the matching Godot .NET SDK.\r\n- Built non-threaded static LibGodot Web debug template.\r\n- Built threaded static LibGodot Web debug template with `proxy_to_pthread=yes`.\r\n- Exported a C# test project with both templates.\r\n- Ran both exports in Chromium.\r\n- Verified managed constructors and `_Ready`, Variant marshalling, cryptography, `HttpClient`, JavaScript imports/exports, and the expected JavaScript → C# return value.\r\n- Verified worker-thread entry and exit in the threaded export under COOP/COEP isolation headers.\r\n- Ran `git diff --check`, Python compile checks, and XML validation for the SDK props/targets.\r\n\r\n## Current limitations\r\n\r\n- Requires Emscripten 3.1.56 until the .NET runtime toolchain moves forward.\r\n- Dynamic GDExtensions are not supported in C# Web exports.\r\n- Godot LTO is not supported for this static library path.\r\n- Exports are slower because every export performs the final native WebAssembly link.\r\n- Threaded exports require cross-origin isolation and inherit .NET browser threading/interop limitations.\r\n- Threaded exports are incompatible with WebXR for the same reason as `proxy_to_pthread`.\r\n\r\nThis remains experimental and is intentionally submitted as a draft.\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-28T19:22:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T09:27:03Z","closed_at":"2026-07-28T19:26:19Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"364ef70ade3dfb76d1172185692786ec4bf2660a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"wpbiggs:work/dotnet-web-libgodot-rebase","ref":"work/dotnet-web-libgodot-rebase","repo":{"id":1315357757,"node_id":"R_kgDOTmbEPQ","name":"godot","full_name":"wpbiggs/godot","owner":{"login":"wpbiggs","id":9951968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTE5Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9951968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs","html_url":"https://github.com/wpbiggs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpbiggs/following{/other_user}","gists